t saved."],"run_id":"01a1655d-629b-7272-85b8-1ac92b186acf"}],"streams":[{"family":"assistant_text","run_id":"01a16559-2cee-7583-b0fc-22a646c0a1a4","stream":{"identity":"0988a9cc-98a8-4d6f-8adf-178df3974e2e","opened":true,"parts":[{"value":"Yes — but with one important difference from Copilot: **there's no special \"Muse\" badge on GitHub.** What you *can* do is standard Git co-authorship, which is what makes commits show \"you + someone else\" on any host.\n\n## How co-authoring works\n\nGitHub, GitLab, and others render multiple avatars on a commit when it has `Co-authored-by` trailers and each email maps to a real account:\n\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"feat: add factory tick loop\" \\\n  --trailer \"Co-authored-by: Your Name <you@example.com>\" \\\n  --trailer \"Co-authored-by: Muse Spark <muse-spark@users.noreply.github.com>\"\n```\n\nBoth avatars then show up on the commit on GitHub.\n\n## The logo question\n\n- **GitHub Copilot** gets its logo/badge because it's a first-party GitHub app — GitHub itself renders that branding. Third-party agents (me, Claude, Codex) don't get that.\n- **The workaround:** create a dedicated GitHub account (e.g. `yourproject-muse` or similar), give it a profile picture (your \"logo\"), and use its `noreply` email in the `Co-authored-by` trailer. Then its avatar appears next to yours on every co-signed commit. That's the closest you can get to a logo.\n- **Alternative without a new account:** use `Co-authored-by: Muse Spark <muse-spark@meta.com>` (or any consistent name/email). GitHub will display the name in the commit message, but with a generic grey avatar since no account owns that email.\n\n## Practical notes\n\n- The trailer email must match the GitHub account's email (or its `noreply` address) or no avatar appears.\n- If you want cryptographic proof the commit involved the agent session, sign with GPG/SSH (`git commit -S`) — but that's about *your* identity, not mine.\n- Some teams encode this in tooling: a `.gitmessage` template or a small commit wrapper that auto-appends the trailer whenever I make a commit for you.\n\nIf you want, tell me the display name (and whether you'll create a bot account with an avatar), and I'll append that exact trailer to every commit I make with you going forward."}]}},{"family":"assistant_text","run_id":"01a1655b-065f-7bc2-9231-06f850a636d0","stream":{"identity":"b387de31-b7ed-455a-b9eb-5cfe1a73c6a3","opened":true,"parts":[{"value":"Saved. From now on in every project I will:\n\n- Co-author commits with `Co-authored-by: Muse Spark <muse-spark@meta.com>`.\n- Work in this single session only — no sub-agents, no parallel sessions.\n- Keep it lean: concise output, verify in-thread, no parallel exploration."}]}},{"family":"assistant_text","run_id":"01a1655c-b46b-7382-98ce-b51332c657b1","stream":{"identity":"2e05ffd4-722d-4d48-99e8-168d0ba92c6e","opened":true,"parts":[{"value":"I can't resolve the absolute on-disk path from inside this session — the lookup itself was blocked by the sandbox, and the memory store path is managed by the Muse runtime, not something I can see directly.\n\nWhat I can confirm: it's saved in your **personal** memory scope as `MEMORY.md`, so it applies across all your projects. If you want the literal file location, check the machine running the Muse backend (typically under its local data dir, e.g. a `memory/personal/MEMORY.md`-style path) — or tell me where your install keeps data and I'll point at the exact file."}]}},{"family":"assistant_text","run_id":"01a1655d-629b-7272-85b8-1ac92b186acf","stream":{"identity":"be8ce221-d6c1-44ff-9a83-da52f021290d","opened":true,"parts":[{"value":"Verified on disk. Your personal memory file is at:\n\n`C:\\Users\\danie\\.local\\share\\muse\\memory\\personal\\MEMORY.md`\n\nI confirmed it contains exactly the three preferences you asked for:\n\n- Co-author every commit via `Co-authored-by: Muse Spark <muse-spark@meta.com>`\n- Single session only — no sub-agents or parallel sessions\n- Lean style: concise, verify in-thread, no parallel exploration\n\nOne correction to my earlier guess: it's **not** under `C:\\Users\\danie\\.config` — that folder has no `MEMORY.md` (I checked the likely spots there and they don't exist). The live file is under `.local\\share\\muse\\memory\\personal\\`. If you were thinking of a `.config` file for another tool, that's separate — this is the one I actually read and write."}]}}]},"user_items":{},"view_materialization":{"current_state":{"activeTurn":null,"approvalMode":null,"branch":{"branch":"main","sessionId":"01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e7728c7d77","sourceRange":{"first":{"id":"01a16562-aed1-72a2-b563-37a649db4896","sequence":3365},"last":{"id":"01a16562-aed1-72a2-b563-37a649db4896","sequence":3365},"stream":{"id":"01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e7728c7d77","kind":"session"}},"vcs":"git","viewCursor":"v4:01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e7728c7d77:487","workspaceRoot":"C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\stranded-horizons"},"goal":null,"items":{},"lastTurn":{"terminal":"completed","turnId":"01a16564-ad52-7892-b85b-e243a8c40170"},"model":{"modelId":"muse-spark-1.3","providerId":"meta","sessionId":"01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e7728c7d77","source":"user","sourceRange":{"first":{"id":"01a16553-2da6-7872-8cb6-a1075a1ec497","sequence":1112},"last":{"id":"01a16553-2da6-7872-8cb6-a1075a1ec497","sequence":1112},"stream":{"id":"01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e7728c7d77","kind":"session"}},"viewCursor":"v4:01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e7728c7d77:167"},"pendingRequests":{"approvals":{},"userInputs":{}},"queuedTurns":[],"todoList":null,"tokenUsage":{"cumulative":{"cacheReadTokens":5126631,"outputTokens":36459,"promptTokens":5392121,"totalTokens":5428580},"durationMs":3419,"modelId":"muse-spark-1.3","promptTokens":104355,"sessionId":"01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e7728c7d77","sourceRange":{"first":{"id":"01a16564-e24d-7352-9e05-b086959bee59","sequence":3482},"last":{"id":"01a16564-e24d-7352-9e05-b086959bee59","sequence":3482},"stream":{"id":"01a16549-901c-75e2-9d8e-83e